# Exact item ids — no colon-family lookups

`questionA:0:1` is **one live instance** of the design item `questionA`.
A follow-up hanging under it is a **different form item** (any type). They
share no inheritance. Parenthood lives in `changes[originId].formItems`,
not in the child’s `header.id`.

Lookups are **exact**. Do not strip `:` / invent `itemIdBase` / scan “same
base” keys. Missing key means missing — not a sibling’s or the design
item’s annotation. That is the model, not a fault-tolerant reader — see
`pure-logic-not-fault-tolerance.mdc`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — follow-up is not an instance of questionA:0
itemIdBase("questionA:0:1-followup-…") === itemIdBase("questionA:0:0")

// ❌ BAD — sibling nested instances share a “base”
itemIdBase("questionA:0:1") === "questionA:0"

// ✅ GOOD
changes[originId]
followUpItems[originId]
old?.values[id]
old?.changes[id]
```

Follow-up `formItem.id` is an opaque unique answer key (`followup-${Date.now()}`).
Do not prefix it with the origin instance path.
